# The core is copied byte for byte under each project's core/ (core.yml compares the two), so no line ending is ever
# converted, here or there: this file travels with the copy.
* -text
# What stays in this repository alone: `git archive`, which makes each project's copy (scripts/sync.mjs), leaves it
# out, and core.yml and scripts/copy-tree.mjs compare a copy with the core without it. Both read these lines, each
# spelled exactly so and named in both: another folder kept here needs both changed first, or every project's check of
# its copy fails. The dated reports, and the record of the owner's word behind the archive (#252); the core's own
# tests, which no project runs (#527).
/reports export-ignore
/words export-ignore
/tests export-ignore
